2026-10-20T22:10:00Z  CLAIM    Windows gate: muxer wrote nothing (mandatory LockFileEx), and the lane could not even say why its tests failed
2026-10-20T22:10:00Z  VERIFY   run 39499466204 (commit d0e4247) reached 15 ctest entries and failed 5 suites with 20 FAIL! lines, all readable for the first time because a failing suite now echoes Qt Test's own `-o file,txt` log to stderr. The decisive line, repeated for every file: "Failed to write header: Permission denied" / "Failed to write the trailer; the file is incomplete: Permission denied". Root cause: VideoRecorderFFmpeg claimed the output with _O_EXCL *and* LockFileEx over the whole file; Windows byte-range locks are mandatory, the muxer writes through a second avio handle, so the claim blocked its own recording. POSIX flock is advisory, which is why macOS and Linux never saw it. Fix: the Windows claim is _O_EXCL alone. Same family, also fixed: DownloadQueue::nativeHandleOf narrowed _get_osfhandle's intptr_t into an int (a truncated handle makes every LockFileEx fail, so every existing part file read as a live writer), and the part path is now unlinked before the claim because Windows CREATE_NEW resolves a dangling reparse point instead of refusing it. Three assertions were separator-specific and now compare canonical paths or file names.
